 "note": "k=3 lines are ANLI's tiebreak subset: the protocol adds a third verifier only when the first two disagree. 'n_tiebreak' counts k=3 lines where the first two genuinely differ AND the writer's gold is one of the two disputed labels, so the third verifier's vote decides whether the gold becomes the strict majority; tiebreak_gold/other/third partition those by whether the third verifier picked the gold, the other first label, or a distinct third label (no majority). 'firsttwo_agree' on a k=3 line is a protocol anomaly (a third verifier was added although the first two already agreed). P1 (structural) bets the first two verifiers differ on >99% of k=3 lines (a finding either way). P2 (directional) bets the third verifier sides with the writer's gold on >50% of genuine tiebreaks. P3 (cross-check) bets gold == strict verifier majority on >99% of all joined lines (reproduces audit 39). This audit measures AGREEMENT, not label correctness."
}